{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310651,"nonce":"5GRjCcETCopcr93SpzNhOFMwi0Q=","title":"TWO fixes, both bare-name collisions on `free`: Cranelift 366197cf, and the LLVM SIBLING 999713b9 (arity comparison omitted the hidden env, ...","message":"Cranelift was guarded in 366197cf; **the LLVM path was not**, and it failed by a\nDIFFERENT mechanism. `declare_function` (llvm_jit_backend.rs) reuses an existing\nsame-name declaration when the arities match, but built its comparison from the\nfunction's USER parameters while reading the other side's REAL ones. A Haxe\nfunction always carries a hidden `env`, so **that condition can only be true when\nthe existing declaration is extern** — `Q8Cache.free()` (receiver only) matched\nlibc `free(ptr)` and bound to it. The body then lowered under the Haxe ABI, whose\nparam walk spends slot 0 on `env`; with one slot available the RECEIVER WAS NEVER\nBOUND.\n\nSYMPTOM (silent, two-stage): `[tier] LLVM upgrade failed: Error in function\n'free' (IrFunctionId(...)): ... IrId(0) not found in LLVM value_map (continuing\non Cranelift)` — then **SIGILL, exit 132**, with the program's own output never\nappearing. Fix = track names declared for the C ABI (`extern_decl_names`) and\ngive a Haxe function its own symbol instead.\n\n**REPRO SHAPE (nonobvious):** needs a Haxe-defined `free()` AND an extern `free()`\ncalled from ONE function body. Each alone passes; two externs together pass.\nBisecting by pairs is what found it.\n\n**TRAPS this cost:** BSD sed has no `\\b` (the range edit silently no-ops — use\nperl); `pins.sh` ends in `exec` so SOURCING it kills the shell, it is a WRAPPER;\na crash before the first print looks like the loader failing — use file markers,\nand note the last marker was inside a call that had ALREADY returned in the\npassing case.\n\nRoot cause was NOT name mangling. In `cranelift_backend.rs`, `malloc`/`realloc`/\n`free` were matched by BARE NAME in three places each: the declare pass SKIPPED\nany MIR function with those names, and a later pass BOUND the MIR id straight to\nthe libc import. A bodied user method therefore landed on an Import declaration,\nwhich cannot be defined.\n\n**Both guards are needed.** Fixing only the bind moves the failure to \"Function\nnot declared\" because the declare pass already skipped it. The fix is\n`function.cfg.blocks.is_empty()` on both — only an EXTERN declaration is the real\nintrinsic. Regression test: `compiler/tests/haxe/test_method_named_free.hx`\n(covers all three names). Suite 175/175.\n\nTRAP while debugging this: a probe placed AFTER an early `return Ok(())` never\nfires, which looks exactly like \"this code path is dead\". Probe the ENTRY.\nAlso `sed -i '' 's/\\bX\\b/Y/g'` silently does nothing on BSD sed (no `\\b`) —\nverify the edit, not the exit code.\n\n```\nWarning: [W0020] cannot compile `nue.transformer.Q8Cache.free`;\n  runtime calls will SIGILL.\n  reason: Failed to define function 'free': Invalid to define identifier\n          declared as an import: free\n```\nEmitted when compiling anything that reaches `nue/nue/transformer/Q8Cache.hx`.\nThe method gets a trap stub, so `cache.free()` is a latent SIGILL — the Q8 KV\ncaches are simply never released.\n\nA method named `free` is lowered to the BARE global symbol `free` instead of\nbeing mangled with its declaring class, so it collides with the libc `free`\nalready declared as an import in the module. Same disease family as the rest of\nthe id-space cluster: a bare name used where an FQN belongs\n([[feedback_fqn_first_resolution]], [[bugs_xmodule_resolution_disease_cluster]]).\n\nAny method whose name matches a libc symbol the module imports is presumably\naffected — `free` is just the one nue happens to hit. `malloc`, `read`,\n`write`, `open`, `close` are the obvious other candidates; NOT yet checked.\n\nIt is silent unless you read the build output: the call compiles, the program\nruns, and the memory is never freed. Found 2026-08-09 while writing\n`nue/tests/flashbatch` — that oracle deliberately does NOT call `Q8Cache.free()`\nand says so inline, so removing the workaround needs this fixed first.\n\nMangle instance/static method symbols with the declaring class FQN at the\ncodegen boundary, so `nue.transformer.Q8Cache.free` never competes for the\nglobal `free`. Verify by disassembly, not by IR\n([[feedback_verify_codegen_by_disasm]]), and check the trap-stub log with\n`RAYZOR_DUMP_FN_PTRS=1` ([[bugs_trap_stub_cascade]]).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_method_named_free_collides_with_libc` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}